Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: xtgeoip
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/HomerSlated/xtgeoip/issues
Source: https://github.com/HomerSlated/xtgeoip
Comment: The orig tarball is rolled with `git archive`, whose export-ignore
 rules drop extra/ — and with it the vendored GPL-2 xtables-addons source
 that would otherwise need its own stanza here. If you add a vendor/
 directory to the orig tarball (debian/README.source explains when you must),
 every crate in it becomes part of the source package and this file has to
 account for all 307 of them. `cargo-lock`, `licensecheck` and
 `cargo-license` are the usual ways to generate that; it is not a small job,
 and it is the main reason to prefer a network-enabled build if you have one.

